# Map annotations: annotation_map

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`annotation_map()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/annotation_map.html), in the order
the page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly
cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a
list of what remains.

`annotation_map()` draws a fixed map on a plot: the outlines in a data frame such as `map_data()`
returns, with a `fill` and `colour` of their own. It predates `geom_sf()` and does not read `sf`
geometry, but it can be drawn alongside `geom_sf()` layers, or in `coord_sf()`, which projects
it. Giggly has none of it yet.

## Cities on a state map

The page's examples run only when the `maps` package is installed, and the last two only when the
`sf` package is too: each `if` opens a brace that closes after the last example.

```r
if (requireNamespace("maps", quietly = TRUE)) {
# location of cities in North Carolina
df <- data.frame(
  name = c("Charlotte", "Raleigh", "Greensboro"),
  lat = c(35.227, 35.772, 36.073),
  long = c(-80.843, -78.639, -79.792)
)

p <- ggplot(df, aes(x = long, y = lat)) +
  annotation_map(
    map_data("state"),
    fill = "antiquewhite", colour = "darkgrey"
  ) +
  geom_point(color = "blue") +
  geom_text(
    aes(label = name),
    hjust = 1.105, vjust = 1.05, color = "blue"
  )

# use without coord_sf() is possible but not recommended
p + xlim(-84, -76) + ylim(34, 37.2)
```

Not in Giggly yet: map data from the `maps` package, `annotation_map()`, `geom_text()` and
mapping `label`, a fixed `fill`, `colour`, `hjust` and `vjust`, and `xlim()` and `ylim()`.

## A projected map

```r
if (requireNamespace("sf", quietly = TRUE)) {
# use with coord_sf() for appropriate projection
p +
  coord_sf(
    crs = sf::st_crs(3347),
    default_crs = sf::st_crs(4326),  # data is provided as long-lat
    xlim = c(-84, -76),
    ylim = c(34, 37.2)
  )
```

Not in Giggly yet: everything `p` needs (map data from the `maps` package, `annotation_map()`,
`geom_text()`), and `coord_sf()`, with coordinate reference systems from the `sf` package.

## Mixing with sf layers

```r
# you can mix annotation_map() and geom_sf()
nc <- sf::st_read(system.file("shape/nc.shp", package = "sf"), quiet = TRUE)
p +
  geom_sf(
    data = nc, inherit.aes = FALSE,
    fill = NA, color = "black", linewidth = 0.1
  ) +
  coord_sf(crs = sf::st_crs(3347), default_crs = sf::st_crs(4326))
}}
```

`sf::st_read()` reads North Carolina's counties from a file that comes with the `sf` package.

Not in Giggly yet: everything `p` needs (map data from the `maps` package, `annotation_map()`,
`geom_text()`), `sf` objects, `geom_sf()` as a layer with data of its own that ignores the plot's
mapping, a fixed `fill`, `colour` and `linewidth`, and `coord_sf()`.
